Z||000000||bHooper||10-08-2001||02:10 PM||||my auto v-6 SE makes a funny noise from time to time.  it appears to be related to rpm's and gear selection.<P>when i let off the throttle to stop, the noise disipates.  <P><BR>could this be the torque convertor, or lock up selonoid creating a "whirring sound"?  the only other symptom is that the car seems to "torque" a bit to the right under acceleration.  not mild and not real heavy aceleration.  <P>i have replaced the tranny mounts, the trany filter and fluid since getting this car.  and i am relatively certain that this problem is coming from the transmission area as i never notice it unless the car is in drive.<P>thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||10-08-2001||10:49 PM||||I don't know if this will help or not.<BR>My 88 coupe auto would make a strange whiring sound when the TC would kick in at about 40ish mph. This is right when it would go into 3rd gear and lock up the TC. When I had my ultimate dog bone in I could feel a vibration everywhere in the car when this would happen.<P>Is this whats happening to you also? I allways thought the torque convertor locked up a little to soon in the 4 cylinders. It would almost bog the engine when it happend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.||||reg||1
