Z||000004||87GTZ34||10-10-2001||10:40 AM||||Hoop,  I have the same or similar noise.  Mine seemed to start when I changed the filter and the cooling hoses in the motor compartment (both at once).  My car will make the noise at idle but it will come & go.  I also hear it during light acceleration.  Under heavy accel, there is too much exhaust noise but it most likely is still there.  The noise actually sounds like a loose shaft inside a bearing, or a loose bearing but it is in sync with the frequency of engine RPMs.  I was thinking of 3 possibilities: torque converter, internal drive chain (or associated hardware), or hydraulic noise from pump or valve body.  It is very weird that this started after I put fresh fluid in it.  I have two faint rattles that make diagnoses tougher...  The AC junction block on the driver’s side is loose, and the muffler shop installed my Borla system and left two spring brackets touching a shield.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||10-11-2001||10:50 AM||||well, i drained the tranny, replaced the filter and put in 3 quarts of fresh ATF.  around the block (per ogre's web page) and so far so good.  <P>i have to run out this afternoon, so that will be the test.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
